    description: "Surfaced by WI-kalug-takiz-lumim-falaj-kopuf-tapor-kizof-sajur's family sweep (2026-09-30, branch jgstern-agent/fix/kalug-ts-interface-extends).\n\nGo interface embedding emits NO edge: `type GChild interface { GBase; N() }` gives GChild meta with no base_classes (only `concepts` and `visibility_signal`), and no extends edge is emitted by the analyzer or the core inheritance linker. go.py records embedding as base_classes for STRUCTS only (struct-embedding branch ~1636/1669).\n\nREPRO: fixture e.go = `package p` / `type GBase interface { M() }` / `type GChild interface { GBase; N() }`; `hypergumbo survey . --out f.json` -> zero extends/implements edges; GChild meta has no base_classes.\n\nlinkers/type_hierarchy.py `_extends_admits_dispatch` docstring states \"Go interface embedding (`type Bar interface { Foo; ... }`) ... produce[s] extends edges between interface symbols\" -- not true on this repro, so the dispatch override that docstring justifies has no Go input. Not measured: whether a Go interface-embedding edge changes dispatches_to on any corpus repo (WI-tudib handles promoted methods for satisfaction separately; check it before fixing).\n\nWith WI-kalug's core change, base_classes on the embedding interface is enough for the core linker to emit GChild -extends-> GBase."  # 7851
