  message: "From WI-nizug-lavig-duhob-finog-mudus-rizut-zidub-jurit (local branch `jgstern-agent/fix/nizug`, commit 8e1e058645, not merged): the `type_hierarchy._extends_admits_dispatch` docstring that claimed Go interface embedding and C# interface inheritance already produce `extends` edges between interface symbols is rewritten there. It now says no deny-list analyzer emits such a hop on the measured fixtures (C# `interface IB : IA`, Go `type RW interface { Reader; ... }`, Rust `trait Solid: Shape` all emit no edge, dev 4dfb1d645a) and names this item. Bearing on this item: once the producer emits the edge, the gate needs no change. With WI-kalug's core linker the edge is labelled `extends` (interface source), and the gate admits it because the child is abstract. Without WI-kalug the edge is `implements`, which the gate never touches. I ran WI-nizug's fixture with WI-kalug's core diff applied: the dispatches_to set was identical, and the only edge that changed was Java `IChild -> IBase` going from implements to extends."  # a543
